# Root .env.example — DEPRECATED, superseded, propose deleting.
#
# Nothing in this repository actually reads a root-level `.env` file.
# Confirmed live: services/api loads `services/api/.env` (pydantic-
# settings, `env_file=".env"` relative to that service's own working
# directory), apps/dashboard loads `apps/dashboard/.env` (Next.js's own
# built-in per-app dotenv loading), and infra/docker loads
# `infra/docker/.env` (docker compose's own --env-file convention). No
# script, no root package.json config, nothing anywhere calls
# `dotenv`/reads a root `.env` (checked: no match for it repo-wide).
#
# This file previously listed variables under an invented naming scheme
# the code has never used — EXCHANGE_* instead of the real DELTA_*,
# JWT_SECRET/JWT_EXPIRATION_MINUTES instead of the real
# JWT_SECRET_KEY/JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES, plus OBJECT_STORAGE_*/
# SMTP_*/REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET, none of which any code in this repo reads
# at all. Following it produced a server that silently failed to
# authenticate to Delta or issue tokens (STATE.md §4, flagged issue #5).
# That content has been removed rather than left to keep drifting.
#
# The real, current, field-by-field-verified templates are:
#   - services/api/.env.example   (106 fields, matches app/core/config.py exactly)
#   - apps/dashboard/.env.example (3 fields, already accurate — no changes needed)
#   - infra/docker/.env.example   (6 fields, already accurate — no changes needed)
#
# See STATE.md §4 for the full audit and Step 2/Step 6 of the follow-up
# task that produced this rewrite. Recommendation: delete this file
# entirely once you've confirmed nothing in your own tooling (outside
# this repo) still points at it — keeping an empty pointer around is
# strictly better than a wrong template, but a fourth file that says
# "look at the other three" is still a fourth file to keep in sync.
